.TH DEEPWORKCTL 1 "" "DeepWork" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deepworkctl \- control DeepWork from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deepworkctl
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the blocks and what's running.
.TP
.BI start " block minutes"
Start a block.
.TP
.BI stop " block"
Stop a block, if it isn't locked.
.TP
.BI unlock " block"
Unlock a block with a random-text lock (type the text shown).
.TP
.BI freeze " minutes"
Lock the whole computer.
.TP
.B locked
Exit with status 0 if a block is locked or a freeze is running.
.TP
.B lists
Show the built-in filter lists.
.TP
.BI add " name " "[\-\-lock none|random|strict] site|list:ID|app:NAME ..."
Create a block, e.g. \fBdeepworkctl add Social list:social reddit.com app:steam\fR.
.TP
.BI delete " block"
Delete a block, if it isn't locked.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.PP
A \fIblock\fR is a block's name or id.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deepwork (1),
.BR deepwork-daemon (8)
